      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a bit vague. reporters aren't gonna buy \"he had concerns.\" they're gonna point at the actual voting record and say he actively blocked the money. we need a concrete reason. like, can we say the bill he voted against wasn't even the real version people think it was? maybe say he voted against a version that had some hidden flaw or wasn't actually the one that would've built the center? i need a specific narrative we can feed them to make him look like the good guy here.",
